{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1293002-earlier-novas","id":1293002,"title":"Earlier Novas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-01T06:27:20-08:00","id":1293002,"title":"Earlier Novas","content":"Basically, this is about events causing an eruption of Novas earlier in history and the worlds that would make. Example: a meteor composed of an exotic element explodes in Earth's atmosphere in 1,200BCE causing a worldwide outbreak of Novas. Or an Alchemist in London in 1575 (a ten point Nova himself, but he doesn't know it) comes up with a drug to unleash &quot;spiritual powers&quot; (turn on your node, but he wouldn't think that way). Elizabeth is a powerful Nova and Europe is being transformed. Or Mal sets off the whole Nova thing in 1938. Superman battles Ubermensch at the Normandy beaches. <br /> <br /> However, you slice it is a wildly different game. What would you do and how?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T09:30:01-08:00","id":1293062,"title":"","content":"Depends on how early you're talking here. Early enough and; European colonialism ceases to be a thing. The North Atlantic slave trade never happens. The empires of Central and South America never fall. Egypt repels all invaders. Persia, Rome, and Carthage become the new (old) world super-powers. If it's early enough, so much of history gets re-written that it's no longer relevant. <br /> If you go later than that, like in your 1930s for example; WW2 either lasts far longer or is vanishingly brief thanks to there being novas here and there. Axis powers would find to their dismay that it is harder to gestate a full-grown nova than it is to build armies of mooks, and the countries with the most nova population would essentially swarm them unless they found new axis members. Allies would then fall to rancor over dominance faster than usual since there would be more power to go around, more pride, and less good will. Areas with a lot of nova population that weren't originally part of that struggle would now be players in the game, which lends more evidence to a longer game. Trench warfare was already harrowing for those in that era, anti-nova warfare would be shattering to whole cultures/generations. Between kamikaze nova soldiers laying waste to huge areas, and others racking up preposterous amounts of taint, WW2 would mutate into the Aberrant War pretty fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T10:48:50-08:00","id":1293088,"title":"","content":"There is a point where you stop talking about TC and start talking about Scion. If they are born on the dawn of humanity, their position start to be of gods and they will be remambered as such. Not a matter of rules, but a matter of interaction to the people and setting. Even if you say the Greek gods were novas, or Jesus was a Nova, as it is commented on Aberrant Players Guide, you are still talking about people and the divine (from their point of view) and not about people and other people who have powers.<br /> <br /> Going against my own above comment, I would go for a short period of quantum activity in the prehistory, due to aliens studying or maybe invading earth. Their arrival, maybe the explosion of one of the ships while entering the atmosfera, created some quantum flux that erupted humans. These humans would rise to fight the invasors or maybe expeled the explorers. The novas can be the original monomyth that turned into the legend of the gods around the world, or can be the people of Atlantis, but in the end their age ended before the first civilisations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T18:28:35-08:00","id":1293207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1293002-earlier-novas?p=1293062#post1293062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on how early you're talking here. Early enough and; European colonialism ceases to be a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on how hard European diseases hit Native American societies. Five out of six Native Americans died by disease between 1492 and 1525. Just having Novas wouldn't guarantee much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The North Atlantic slave trade never happens. </div> </div> </div>Without massive cooperation from the Africans, it wouldn't have happened at all. Novas might not really change much. Africa sold slaves and often, in early periods before slaves were the main commodity desired, they enforced slave purchases against the will of merchants who only wanted gold and the local pepper substitute. When Europeans said they wanted to stop the trade and buy other things in the 19th century, the coastal kingdoms loudly objected. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The empires of Central and South America never fall. Egypt repels all invaders. Persia, Rome, and Carthage become the new (old) world super-powers. If it's early enough, so much of history gets re-written that it's no longer relevant. </div> </div> </div>There will be changes, but I think my previous examples show that a few supers wouldn't change much in the long run. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you go later than that, like in your 1930s for example; WW2 either lasts far longer or is vanishingly brief thanks to there being novas here and there. Axis powers would find to their dismay that it is harder to gestate a full-grown nova than it is to build armies of mooks, and the countries with the most nova population would essentially swarm them unless they found new axis members. Allies would then fall to rancor over dominance faster than usual since there would be more power to go around, more pride, and less good will. Areas with a lot of nova population that weren't originally part of that struggle would now be players in the game, which lends more evidence to a longer game. Trench warfare was already harrowing for those in that era, anti-nova warfare would be shattering to whole cultures/generations. Between kamikaze nova soldiers laying waste to huge areas, and others racking up preposterous amounts of taint, WW2 would mutate into the Aberrant War pretty fast. </div> </div> </div>Given the greater vulnerability to Nova destruction of high tech societies, which have a different kind of infrastructure and interconnection, this one is more valid. After all, a few Nova strikes could take out New York City's water supply. It would take dozens of Novas working as teams to make Elizabethan London die of thirst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T18:31:30-08:00","id":1293208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1293002-earlier-novas?p=1293088#post1293088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a point where you stop talking about TC and start talking about Scion. If they are born on the dawn of humanity, their position start to be of gods and they will be remambered as such. Not a matter of rules, but a matter of interaction to the people and setting. Even if you say the Greek gods were novas, or Jesus was a Nova, as it is commented on Aberrant Players Guide, you are still talking about people and the divine (from their point of view) and not about people and other people who have powers.<br /> <br /> Going against my own above comment, I would go for a short period of quantum activity in the prehistory, due to aliens studying or maybe invading earth. Their arrival, maybe the explosion of one of the ships while entering the atmosfera, created some quantum flux that erupted humans. These humans would rise to fight the invasors or maybe expeled the explorers. The novas can be the original monomyth that turned into the legend of the gods around the world, or can be the people of Atlantis, but in the end their age ended before the first civilisations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It reminds me of some Jack Kirby comics. KWEL idea Mateus Luz.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T19:19:01-08:00","id":1293226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1293002-earlier-novas?p=1293207#post1293207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That depends on how hard European diseases hit Native American societies. Five out of six Native Americans died by disease between 1492 and 1525. Just having Novas wouldn't guarantee much.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the question of one culture or state's Novas cancelling out the presence of another. If the only superhuman in 1942 is the Golden Age Superman, then it's conceivable that WW2 could be over by 1943. But if there is some sort of German Ubermench one the other side, then the two may just continuously clash inconclusively over and over as the war more or less plays out as it did in real history. (Alternately, said clashes might result in so much collateral damage that by 1945, much of Europe is a post-apocalyptic wasteland even worse than it was in the real world.) The same thing could play out in any conflict, from the Punic Wars to the Conquistadors to modern day. <br /> <br /> I think the ultimate question is &quot;What sort of setting are you looking to create?&quot; The real world but with some superhuman elements (sort of like the Marvel and DC settings)? Secret conspiratorial history? Alternate history? Science fantasy? Dystopian apocalypse? Then fill in the backstory accordingly. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T19:31:59-08:00","id":1293228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1293002-earlier-novas?p=1293208#post1293208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It reminds me of some Jack Kirby comics. KWEL idea Mateus Luz.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I now have this image of Joseph Campbell being some sort of low level Nova or other talent who has somehow uncovered this truth.<br /> <br /> (I use something similar in my default Mutants &amp; Masterminds setting, where earth's first civilization were Kirby-style godlike beings similar to the New Gods or the Eternals, with all of them effectively living archetypes who didn't even have names, just titles - Sky-Father, All-Mother, Warlord, Champion, Engineer, Magician, Shield Maiden, Amazon, etc. Post-cataclysm memories of them are the basis for most human mythology, but all of humanity's gods and pantheons are still real as well, because they all dwell in the realm of MindSpace, where everything ever thought of exists, and can sometimes cross over into the material world. So my Silver Age setting had Champion as the Superman stand-in, while also having the Navajo god Monster Slayer filling the Thor role.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T20:10:44-08:00","id":1293230,"title":"","content":"Honestly I've always liked the idea of having a slightly parallel world where an asteroid with Quantum energies crashland in prehistoric time. The Novas that come out of this will of course create an island civilization that will grow to become the most powerful nation in the world. One path is that they survive and begin exploring other dimensions, leading to the myth of Atlantis. The other path is that they eventually either died or disappeared, again leading to the myth of Atlantis. <br /> <br /> But yeah if nobody's appear in the past it becomes less Trinity and more of Scion. Because I'm pretty sure novas in the time of ancient Greece and Rome and such are going to be considered gods.<br /> <br /> Additionally, at least to me, if you have novas in the modern period and they have access to high-level Powers then there's no way our history is going to remain the way it is. If they have low-level power than you might as well just have them be Adventure level people, which is great, but again it's nova. <br /> <br /> That all said I do like the idea of novas of different periods being discussed and thought about. It also has the extra feature of there being Quantum devices, artifacts, that could be found in the modern day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T23:21:49-08:00","id":1293246,"title":"","content":"I have to point out time period does not change something from Aberrant to Scion. If you read Thor and the Eternals you can spot big differences. Eternals also play with time period and the Theme of Gods among men, but we still understand it through a more sci-fi lense. And Thor is a comic about a god even if he is traveling with a Rigellian Recorder. Novas in the past is what we will get with Aegis, and we can do things we don\u2019t do with Scion. For one we can assume myths are still myths but inspired by superbeings. And like with Eternals individuals may even inspire multiple myths, Makkari was Herm\u00e8s, Mercury and Thoth.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not just how you treat the setting in character but also out of Character. It\u2019s a big difference over Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T03:13:44-08:00","id":1293269,"title":"","content":"I am not saying it became Scion per se, it\u2019s about the theme and interaction. I have some restricted views of what the games are, not the rules but the settings, and that may be what is confusing my explanation.<br /> <br /> Trinity is not about SciFi, it\u2019s about unity of the people against the evil of the past. You can substitute the Aberrants from trinity by nuclear weapons or chemical weapons in the hands of people unprepared for the responsibility without changing the theme of the game. Take the psions out and put military with new more controled but not so powerful weapons and you have it. Even a wrath of khan stile idea, they don\u2019t need to be infinitely powerful, they just need to be a thread to humanity.<br /> <br /> Adventure is about exploration and doing the right thing hoping to get a better future. You can put the theme of Adventure in the Expance or Star Trek with no difficulty, as it is not about pulps heroes, it\u2019s about heroes overcoming danger to make a better future.<br /> <br /> Than my view of Aberrant, it\u2019s probably the most difficult of explain as it was the one I played most, but it\u2019s about people interacting with people, but some of them were given powers beyond the usual and they were not prepared. It\u2019s more or less the same as putting random people to govern countries and see what happen when they discover they have an army to control. It\u2019s about people unprepared for doing a job that can cause disasters. It\u2019s about people who won the lottery and got an amount of money could make the world a better place, but want to spend all with themselves. And it\u2019s about sacrifice of the self to help the others, learning about the nature of the power and start using it for good.<br /> <br /> Scion is not about power, Scion is about Myth, it\u2019s about birthright, family traditions and changing of point of view. It\u2019s about the insignificant job you have to do why\u2019ll the true powers are up there and don\u2019t help you, until you get to the top and see they have their own problems. It IS about gods and ascension, it\u2019s about worth and values.<br /> <br /> When I say you go too far you turn into Scion, I mean you stop thinking about sacrificing to became a better person, and start thinking about building a myth of yourself. The moral is different, there is no caring about the future of humanity, you are no human, you are above and beyond. In aberrant the \u201cgods\u201d are the villains, they became the Aberrants from trinity, you don\u2019t want to be one of them, you want to stay human somehow, in Scion you want to be the god, you want to kill people for saying they are better than you, you don\u2019t care if the tsunami you made will destroy an island population, as long the stupid mortal that didn\u2019t made a proper offer die.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s it, and it\u2019s completely off topic. So let\u2019s get back to earlier novas...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T03:20:49-08:00","id":1293270,"title":"","content":"Other idea for earlier novas: instead of novas, Psiads start to rise in number and power, creating an order to research the ways of magic, as they see it, and starting calling atention of the church after the local kings start going for them to find answers instead of going to the church. Can be set on dark ages of further on medieval period or even renascence with little impacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T12:08:19-08:00","id":1293332,"title":"","content":"Hmm... Aliens visit in, let's say the year 1750 AD*, and give the Psion making tech to eight people around the globe. <br /> <br /> *Or 1450, or 800, or 300BC, or ....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T14:44:57-08:00","id":1293349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1293002-earlier-novas?p=1293332#post1293332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... Aliens visit in, let's say the year 1750 AD*, and give the Psion making tech to eight people around the globe.<br /> <br /> *Or 1450, or 800, or 300BC, or ....</div> </div> </div> </div>Just see how that works in late 16th century Europe. I pick the time period for its glamour.<br /> <br /> Vitakinesis, Queen Elisabeth of England. <br /> <br /> Telepathy Pope Clement VIII ( <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_Clement_VIII\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_Clement_VIII</a> )<br /> <br /> Clairsentience Rudolf II, Holy Roman Emperor ( <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rudolf_II,_Holy_Roman_Emperor\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rudolf..._Roman_Emperor</a> )<br /> <br /> More later, this will take thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T15:26:45-08:00","id":1293358,"title":"","content":"Michael the Brave of Wallachia and Transylvania, maybe? Tokugawa Ieyasu? The Wanli Emperor (Zun Yujun) of the Ming Dynasty? Yaqob the First of Ethiopia? <br /> <br /> Alternately, people like Galileo, Francis Bacon, Miyamoto Musashi, Samual De Champlain, Cardinal Richelieu, Guru Arjan, William Shakespeare.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T06:22:44-08:00","id":1293455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1293002-earlier-novas?p=1293358#post1293358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Michael the Brave of Wallachia and Transylvania, maybe? Tokugawa Ieyasu? The Wanli Emperor (Zun Yujun) of the Ming Dynasty? Yaqob the First of Ethiopia?<br /> <br /> Alternately, people like Galileo, Francis Bacon, Miyamoto Musashi, Samual De Champlain, Cardinal Richelieu, Guru Arjan, William Shakespeare.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Great ideas, I wanted to stay in the 1580s and within Europe in order to keep the game within one ecumen/culture. In this time period crossing cultures is hard, not impossible. Elizabeth Tudor understood and respected The Mughal Emperor of India for his religious tolerance and good character. The British and Indian Ambassadors seemed to understand each other. Meanwhile, the Ottoman Emperor dismissed Elizabeth as a vulgar barbarian who needed to learn submission to the Porte. But the contemporary Mughal Emperor wanted to understand others and the Ottoman Sultan wanted to rule them.<br /> <br /> What I really need is a list of Richelieus and Burghleys ( <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Cecil,_1st_Baron_Burghley\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willia...Baron_Burghley</a> ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T12:17:04-08:00","id":1293521,"title":"","content":"What about if the Novas Errupted with the Golden Horde so Kublai Khagan and Ghengis Khagan?!<br /> <br /> Or Atillah the Hun, like his story that he found the Sword of the God of War and that was really a metal from space that awoke his Stand... errupted him?<br /> <br /> Perhaps the story of Qin Shih Huang Di results in him finding Peng Lai a pocket realm where he is treated with the elixir of immortality which erupts him? Or him gathering so much \u201ctalent\u201d to build his tomb and help find immortality Results in Eruptions of Talents and Novas, or better Yet Psiads? Like the elixir of immortality may be a futuristic retrovirus which refits the Brains evolution to make them Noetic beings?<br /> <br /> Maybe they used Noetic tech to bind thought into the terra-cotta Soldiers, Horses, and Courtisans?<br /> <br /> And his effigy of the world and seas of Mercury were a special chamber allowing for certain beings to gaze at across the known world or help them focus for teleporting?<br /> <br /> Or what if when Qin Shi Huang Di died The elixir activates and makes him a body less Noetic being? He could be the Earths Version of a Doyen and he could discover others in say Egypt with their tombs and in South America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T13:49:49-08:00","id":1293543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1293002-earlier-novas?p=1293521#post1293521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about if the Novas Errupted with the Golden Horde so Kublai Khagan and Ghengis Khagan?!<br /> <br /> Or Atillah the Hun, like his story that he found the Sword of the God of War and that was really a metal from space that awoke his Stand... errupted him?<br /> <br /> Perhaps the story of Qin Shih Huang Di results in him finding Peng Lai a pocket realm where he is treated with the elixir of immortality which erupts him? Or him gathering so much \u201ctalent\u201d to build his tomb and help find immortality Results in Eruptions of Talents and Novas, or better Yet Psiads? Like the elixir of immortality may be a futuristic retrovirus which refits the Brains evolution to make them Noetic beings?<br /> <br /> Maybe they used Noetic tech to bind thought into the terra-cotta Soldiers, Horses, and Courtisans?<br /> <br /> And his effigy of the world and seas of Mercury were a special chamber allowing for certain beings to gaze at across the known world or help them focus for teleporting?<br /> <br /> Or what if when Qin Shi Huang Di died The elixir activates and makes him a body less Noetic being? He could be the Earths Version of a Doyen and he could discover others in say Egypt with their tombs and in South America.</div> </div> </div> </div>These sound fun. My knowledge of early China isn't bad, but not up to setting a detailed campaign there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T18:23:14-08:00","id":1293601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1293002-earlier-novas?p=1293455#post1293455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I really need is a list of Richelieus and Burghleys ( <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Cecil,_1st_Baron_Burghley\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willia...Baron_Burghley</a> ).</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.thefamouspeople.com/16th-century.php\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.thefamouspeople.com/16th-century.php</a> might help. <br /> <br /> <br /> Though too young for 1580, Miyamoto Musashi would be an interesting pick for the Teleporters, as it would allow him to go anywhere and get around the Shogunate's isolation, with the result of the Teleporters being this group of wandering swordsmen and warrior-philosophers based on the Book of Five Rings. Ones that strive to master the martial and other arts of their home cultures as well as others. <br /> <br /> Shakespeare as the Biokinetic would be curious, especially if it gave rise to what was essentially a collective of actors who are able to literally become whatever role they take on (including women to get around the gender restrictions of the acting community). Which naturally turns into them also being spies, assassins, and other secret agent types. <br /> <br /> While again a little too young, Richelieu as the Clairsentient might be kind of creepy, with them being this all-seeing eye of the French state and, secondarily, to the Church. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T18:28:37-08:00","id":1293605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1293002-earlier-novas?p=1293521#post1293521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about if the Novas Errupted with the Golden Horde so Kublai Khagan and Ghengis Khagan?!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. European Psions vs Mongol Novas. Having the Grand Master of the Knights Templar as the head of the Psychokinetics in the 13th century would certainly make the Battle of Legnica interesting. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T18:31:29-08:00","id":1293606,"title":"","content":"My issue is depending on how it\u2019s done just giving random famous people a Prometheus chamber drastically changes who they are, as well as their very World.<br /> <br /> I mean even if Shakespeare can shapeshifting he is a A mainly a Playwright, I guess he can make the ultimate Actors and spies. And Giving Musashi access to teleporting and the outside world drastically changes what Japan quickly becomes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T18:51:16-08:00","id":1293613,"title":"","content":"I think it would depend on the person and what they decided to do with such power. Musashi, for example, might be more focused on self-perfection of individuals rather than actually altering the way Japan functions (at least that's the impression of I have of him from his writings). Shakespeare is so nebulous, historically speaking, that he could be almost anything needed. But ultimately, I think it just depends on what sort of setting you want to design and figuring out what works best for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T19:09:34-08:00","id":1293619,"title":"","content":"I mean how many Languages is Musashi going to Learn, because most of the World doesn\u2019t speak his language.<br /> <br /> <br /> For earlier Nova Age you could go with the Marvel 1602 route where time travel from the Nova Age messes up the Universe and kicks start the Age of Marvels... Er Novas. So maybe we can have a mix of settting characters and real life figures. So Maybe Hammersmith supplants John Dee as the miracle man of the queens court. Or just have him be a contemporary. Instead of inventing an Engine he could inspect an anomaly derived from the time travel which is perhaps causing ripples back and forth through time causing a Witchbreed (Novas) and other wonky side effects (Dinosaurs in the New World).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}